        "original_id": "2076ebfe-3346-5329-a639-9c87251f97ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Heavenly Creatures\n- People: Peter Jackson, Fran Walsh, Pauline Parker, Juliet Hulme, Anne Perry\n- Events: Parker–Hulme murder case\n- Places: Christchurch, New Zealand\n- Topics: historical detective fiction\n\nFacts:\n- In 1954, the Parker–Hulme murder case occurred in Christchurch, New Zealand.\n- The Parker–Hulme murder case involved teenage girls Pauline Parker and Juliet Hulme murdering Parker's mother.\n- Anne Perry was born as Juliet Marion Hulme on 28 October 1938.\n- In 1994, Heavenly Creatures was released as a New Zealand psychological drama.\n- Peter Jackson directed Heavenly Creatures and co-wrote its screenplay with Fran Walsh.\n- Heavenly Creatures is about the 1954 Parker–Hulme murder case and centers on the relationship between Pauline Parker and Juliet Hulme.\n- Anne Perry is an English author of historical detective fiction best known for the Thomas Pitt and William Monk series.",
